  "id": "knowledge-of-performance",
  "term": "knowledge of performance",
  "definition": "Knowledge of performance is augmented feedback about how a movement was carried out, often given through video replay and specific technique cues to help refine and stabilize skill execution. In motor learning, it focuses on movement quality and can support learners’ error detection and correction as they develop a skill.",
